      "questionType": "text",
      "question": "Explain how the Plan-Do-Check-Act (PDCA) cycle creates a continuous improvement feedback loop.",
      "maxScore": 15,
      "timeLimit": 300,
      "correctAnswer": "The PDCA cycle creates a continuous improvement feedback loop where each phase feeds into the next. Plan establishes goals and methods, Do implements the plan, Check measures results against objectives, and Act standardizes successful improvements or adjusts the plan based on findings. This creates a balancing feedback loop that continuously refines processes, where the Act phase feeds back into the Plan phase for the next iteration, creating ongoing quality improvement.",
